internal fun readerNode001127(): InlineContent.Text = InlineContent.Text(text = "Technical explanation · Head restraints.")
internal fun readerNode001128(): InlineContent.Strong = InlineContent.Strong(children = listOf(readerNode001127()))
internal fun readerNode001129(): InlineContent.Text = InlineContent.Text(text = " In a rear impact, the seat and torso can move while the head lags behind. A correctly designed and adjusted head restraint helps limit damaging head movement relative to the torso and reduce neck-injury risk. Trafikverket advises positioning the top at the crown of the head and keeping the gap behind the head as small as possible. Adjust it for the occupant before driving; a comfort setting is not the same as a protective setting. A head restraint cannot guarantee that injury will be avoided. ")
